cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Groundhog in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Groundhog"
abstract: >-
  Groundhog turns a repository's own commit history into a verified benchmark for
  coding agents. Commits that change source and tests together are
  mined as candidate tasks, then validated by running the test suite twice: once
  without the original fix, where it must fail, and once with it, where it must
  pass. Because tasks are derived from commits, a repository's recent history
  yields evaluation data that postdates a model's training cutoff.
authors:
